 "caveats": [
  "The NPI Registry API returns at most 1,200 records per query (limit 200, skip up to 1000). States that hit the cap are marked capped:true and carry NO count.",
  "The API has no taxonomy-code filter; queries use the taxonomy description and results are then filtered to providers that actually list the exact code.",
  "The API's state filter matches any address on the record (mailing or practice). 'providers_practice_location_in_state' keeps only those whose practice LOCATION address is in the state and is the recommended figure; 'providers_with_taxonomy_code' is the wider count.",
  "A provider with addresses in two states can be counted in both.",
  "NPI taxonomy is self-reported and is not board certification. Records are rarely removed when clinicians retire or move, so counts overstate the active workforce. Trainees and clinicians who list the code as a secondary taxonomy are included unless the 'primary_taxonomy' figure is used.",
  "Individual providers only (NPI-1). Includes DC and Puerto Rico."
 ],
